-- re-embed marker: 2026-06-01u — v0.15.55 Cycle 7 F1: cross-axis HEIGHT fill in row parents (`heightFillFor AsRow`) strips the `height: 100%` emission, keeping only `align-self: stretch;`. Per CSS Flexbox §9.8 the `100%` was redundant when the row's cross-axis (height) was definite AND ACTIVELY HARMFUL when it was flex-grow-derived (indefinite) — the `100%` collapses to auto/content, defeating the stretch and producing the user-reported 22 px / 51 px collapses in #63 (three-pane app shell + Input.multiline). Asymmetric scope: cross-axis WIDTH fill in column / el / textColumn parents KEEPS the `width: 100%` because column-parent widths are typically definite (block inheritance from <body>) AND the explicit `width: 100%` protects against the F4 interaction (`[Ui.width fill, Ui.centerX]` where `align-self: center` cascades over the stretch, leaving width to fall back to content). Width-fill in row parents (main axis) is unchanged: `flex-grow + min-width: 0`. Touches `heightFillFor` in `sky-stdlib/Std/Ui.sky` only. Regression: scripts/verify-stdui-matrix.mjs (Z2 textarea ≥ 760 px tall, Z3 sidebar/main/content ≥ 700 px) + UiFillCssSpec.hs.
-- re-embed marker: 2026-06-01v — v0.15.56 Cycle 7 F3+F4+F5 bundle. F3 (Ui.layoutWith): additive entry point `layoutWith { wrapperAttrs, rootAttrs } : Element msg -> any` lets callers reach the outer 100vh page wrapper — `wrapperAttrs` route Background.color / Font.color / Font.family / html attrs onto the wrapper, `rootAttrs` keep `Ui.layout`'s semantics for the inner root element. `Ui.layout attrs el = Ui.layoutWith { wrapperAttrs = [], rootAttrs = attrs } el` (byte-identical for existing callers). F4 (align-self single-emission): cross-axis fill emitters (`widthFillFor AsColumn/AsEl/AsTextColumn` + `heightFillFor AsRow`) drop the redundant `align-self: stretch` emission — `stretch` is the default `align-items` value, so emitting it explicitly was a no-op AND created cascade-order-dependent rendering when combined with explicit alignment attrs (`Ui.centerX/Y` / `alignLeft/Right/Top/Bottom`). Post-F4 invariant: at most ONE `align-self` declaration per element, sourced from `alignSelfX/Y` only. F1 width-axis stays asymmetric (`width: 100%` KEPT) because the showcase outer column pattern `[Ui.width (Ui.maximum 760 Ui.fill), Ui.centerX]` needs explicit `width: 100%` to survive the alignment cascade (alignment overrides the default stretch; width: 100% stays put so the column fills before centring within the max-width cap). F5 (wrappedRow + spacing): VERIFIED CLEAN at HEAD — wrappedRow uses gap-based spacing (`Ui.spacing N` → `gap: Npx`), wraps cleanly with even row+column spacing. F5 dropped from bundle (no bug to fix). Regression: scripts/verify-stdui-matrix.mjs (F3 + F4 + F5 cells added) + UiAlignSelfSpec.hs + UiFillCssSpec.hs (extended).
